    "note": "Introduced version; no votes on file. Subsection (3) of the section adds treble damages for terrorism or for victims who are disabled, 65 or older, under 16, or targeted as a minority."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (new): A person or public body that creates a gun-free zone is liable for damages resulting from a person felony or person Class A misdemeanor, as those terms are defined in the rules of the Oregon Criminal Justice Commission, committed against an individual in the gun-free zone, if a reasonable person would believe that possession of a firearm could have helped the individual defend against the felony or misdemeanor."
